# Storybook Configuration Skill

## Overview

This skill generates Storybook configurations for React projects using Vite. It includes standard Storybook addons, basic design system integration, and foundational testing setup.

## When to Use This Skill

Use this skill when:
- Setting up Storybook 9 in a new React + Vite project
- Adding basic component documentation and testing
- Integrating with common design systems like Material UI
- Configuring a simple accessibility checking addon

## Quick Start

```bash
# Detect project framework
bash ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/detect-framework.sh

# Use skill to generate configuration
```

## Configuration Generation

### Supported Setup

| Framework | Storybook Package | Version | Bundler |
|-----------|------------------|---------|---------|
| React | `@storybook/react-vite` | 9.0 | Vite |

### Default Patterns

**1. Autodocs Enabled**
```typescript
// main.ts
docs: {
  autodocs: true, // Generate docs for all stories
}
```

**2. Basic Accessibility Addon**
```typescript
// preview.ts
parameters: {
  a11y: {
    element: '#storybook-root',
  },
}
```

**3. Standard Controls**
```typescript
// preview.ts
controls: {
  expanded: false, // Collapsed by default
}
```

## Design System Integration

### Material UI Integration

```typescript
// preview.ts
import { ThemeProvider, createTheme } from '@mui/material/styles';
import CssBaseline from '@mui/material/CssBaseline';

const theme = createTheme({
  palette: {
    mode: 'light', // Fixed light theme
  },
});

export const decorators = [
  (Story) => (
    <ThemeProvider theme={theme}>
      <CssBaseline />
      <Story />
    </ThemeProvider>
  ),
];
```

## Testing Configuration

### Interaction Tests (Playwright)

```typescript
// Install Playwright addon
npm install --save-dev @storybook/addon-playwright
```

### Accessibility Checks

```typescript
// Install a11y addon
npx storybook@latest add @storybook/addon-a11y
```

## Configuration Templates

### React with TypeScript (Storybook 9)

```typescript
// .storybook/main.ts
import type { StorybookConfig } from '@storybook/react-vite';

const config: StorybookConfig = {
  stories: ['../src/**/*.mdx', '../src/**/*.stories.@(js|jsx|mjs|ts|tsx)'],
  addons: [
    '@storybook/addon-essentials', // Includes actions, controls, docs, backgrounds
    '@storybook/addon-a11y',
  ],
  framework: {
    name: '@storybook/react-vite',
    options: {},
  },
  docs: {
    autodocs: true,
  },
};

export default config;
```

```typescript
// .storybook/preview.ts
import type { Preview } from '@storybook/react-vite';
import '../src/index.css';

const preview: Preview = {
  parameters: {
    actions: { argTypesRegex: '^on[A-Z].*' },
    controls: {
      expanded: false,
    },
    layout: 'centered',
  },
};

export default preview;
```

### Sample Story

```tsx
// src/components/Button.stories.tsx
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/react';
import Button from './Button';

const meta: Meta<typeof Button> = {
  title: 'Components/Button',
  component: Button,
  tags: ['autodocs'],
};

export default meta;

type Story = StoryObj<typeof Button>;

export const Primary: Story = {
  args: {
    variant: 'contained',
    children: 'Click me',
  },
};
```

## Quality Checklist

- [ ] Framework detected correctly (React + Vite)
- [ ] Correct Storybook 9 packages installed
- [ ] Basic theme decorator added (if needed)
- [ ] Example story generated

## Best Practices

### Do's
- Use Storybook 9 for stable, widely‑tested configuration
- Enable autodocs for automatic documentation
- Keep controls collapsed to reduce UI clutter
- Add a11y addon as a standard quality gate

### Don'ts
- Don't use advanced platform mocks (e.g., Tauri, Electron)
- Don't configure performance optimizations (they are rarely needed)
- Don't add complex interaction testing addons without explicit requirement

