# Storybook Configuration Skill

## Overview

This skill generates production-ready Storybook configurations for React applications using:
- Storybook 8 with Webpack-based bundling (stable, widely adopted)
- React component library scaffolding
- Accessibility testing with axe-core
- Interaction testing with Jest + Testing Library
- Design system integration (Material UI, Chakra UI, etc.)
- Custom decorators for themes and providers

## When to Use This Skill

This skill should be used when:
- Setting up Storybook in an existing React project
- Upgrading from older Storybook versions (6.x → 8.x)
- Configuring comprehensive testing infrastructure
- Integrating a UI framework like Material UI or Ant Design

## Quick Start

```bash
# Detect project framework and install Storybook
npx storybook@latest init --builder webpack5 --type react

# Add required addons
npx storybook@latest add @storybook/addon-a11y
npx storybook@latest add @storybook/addon-jest
```

## Configuration Generation

### Supported Frameworks

| Framework | Storybook Package | Minimum Version | Bundler |
|-----------|------------------|----------------|---------|
| React | `@storybook/react` | 18.0.0 | Webpack 5 |
| Vue | Not recommended | – | – |
| Svelte | Under development | – | – |

> **Note:** Webpack is the default and most reliable bundler for Storybook. Vite support is experimental.

### Core Configuration Patterns

**1. Interaction Testing with Jest**
```typescript
// .storybook/main.ts
addons: [
  '@storybook/addon-jest', // Jest test results in Storybook
]

// story.test.tsx
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';

test('button click', async () => {
  render(<MyComponent />);
  await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button'));
  expect(screen.getByText('Clicked')).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

**2. Accessibility Testing**
```typescript
// .storybook/preview.ts
parameters: {
  a11y: {
    element: '#storybook-root',
    config: {
      rules: [
        { id: 'color-contrast', enabled: true },
        { id: 'button-name', enabled: true },
      ],
    },
  },
}
```

**3. Automatic Documentation**
```typescript
// .storybook/main.ts
docs: {
  autodocs: 'tag', // Stories with 'autodocs' tag get docs
}
```

**4. Controls Configuration**
```typescript
// .storybook/preview.ts
controls: {
  matchers: {
    color: /(background|color)$/i,
    date: /Date$/i,
  },
  expanded: false, // Keep collapsed by default for performance
}
```

## Theme Integration

### Material UI Decorator

```typescript
// .storybook/preview.ts
import { ThemeProvider, createTheme } from '@mui/material/styles';
import CssBaseline from '@mui/material/CssBaseline';

const lightTheme = createTheme({ palette: { mode: 'light' } });
const darkTheme = createTheme({ palette: { mode: 'dark' } });

export const decorators = [
  (Story, context) => {
    const theme = context.globals.theme === 'dark' ? darkTheme : lightTheme;
    return (
      <ThemeProvider theme={theme}>
        <CssBaseline />
        <Story />
      </ThemeProvider>
    );
  },
];

export const globalTypes = {
  theme: {
    name: 'Theme',
    description: 'Global theme',
    defaultValue: 'light',
    toolbar: {
      icon: 'circlehollow',
      items: ['light', 'dark'],
    },
  },
};
```

### Ant Design Decorator
```typescript
import { ConfigProvider } from 'antd';

export const decorators = [
  (Story) => (
    <ConfigProvider>
      <Story />
    </ConfigProvider>
  ),
];
```

## Testing Infrastructure

### Unit & Interaction Tests
- Uses Jest + Testing Library (standard for React)
- Results displayed in Storybook UI via addon-jest
- Coverage reports via Jest's built-in coverage

### Accessibility Tests
- Configured via `@storybook/addon-a11y`
- Run automatically on every story
- Export results for CI (optional)

### Visual Regression Testing
- Use Chromatic or Percy (not configured here – requires external account)
- Recommended: run Chromatic after each Storybook build

## Configuration Templates

### React with TypeScript (Stable)

```typescript
// .storybook/main.ts
import type { StorybookConfig } from '@storybook/react-webpack5';

const config: StorybookConfig = {
  stories: ['../src/**/*.stories.@(js|jsx|ts|tsx)'],
  addons: [
    '@storybook/addon-links',
    '@storybook/addon-essentials', // Actions, Controls, Docs, Viewport, etc.
    '@storybook/addon-a11y',
    '@storybook/addon-jest', // For interaction test results
  ],
  framework: {
    name: '@storybook/react-webpack5',
    options: {},
  },
  docs: {
    autodocs: 'tag',
  },
  webpackFinal: async (config) => {
    // Custom Webpack config if needed
    return config;
  },
};

export default config;
```

```typescript
// .storybook/preview.ts
import type { Preview } from '@storybook/react';
import '../src/index.css';
import { ThemeProvider, createTheme } from '@mui/material/styles';
import CssBaseline from '@mui/material/CssBaseline';

const lightTheme = createTheme({ palette: { mode: 'light' } });
const darkTheme = createTheme({ palette: { mode: 'dark' } });

const preview: Preview = {
  parameters: {
    actions: { argTypesRegex: '^on[A-Z].*' },
    controls: {
      matchers: {
        color: /(background|color)$/i,
        date: /Date$/i,
      },
      expanded: false,
    },
    layout: 'centered',
    a11y: {
      config: {
        rules: [
          { id: 'color-contrast', enabled: true },
          { id: 'button-name', enabled: true },
        ],
      },
    },
    backgrounds: {
      default: 'light',
      values: [
        { name: 'light', value: '#ffffff' },
        { name: 'dark', value: '#1a1a1a' },
      ],
    },
  },
  globalTypes: {
    theme: {
      description: 'Global theme',
      defaultValue: 'light',
      toolbar: {
        title: 'Theme',
        icon: 'circlehollow',
        items: ['light', 'dark'],
        dynamicTitle: true,
      },
    },
  },
  decorators: [
    (Story, context) => {
      const theme = context.globals.theme === 'dark' ? darkTheme : lightTheme;
      return (
        <ThemeProvider theme={theme}>
          <CssBaseline />
          <Story />
        </ThemeProvider>
      );
    },
  ],
};

export default preview;
```

## Performance Tips

- Keep controls collapsed by default (`expanded: false`)
- Use `stories` patterns to limit scanned files
- Disable docs addon only for very large projects (not recommended)
- Webpack 5 with persistent caching (set `cache.type: 'filesystem'`)

## Quality Checklist

Before completing configuration:
- [ ] Storybook 8 installed with correct framework package
- [ ] Webpack 5 configured (no Vite fallback)
- [ ] Theme decorator added (if using MUI/Ant Design)
- [ ] a11y addon configured
- [ ] Jest test results enabled
- [ ] Autodocs with tag-based generation
- [ ] Example story written
- [ ] package.json scripts: `storybook`, `build-storybook`
- [ ] README created

## Best Practices

### Do's
- Use `npx storybook@latest` for stable releases
- Configure a11y from the start
- Write interaction tests for every story
- Keep addons minimal (only essentials + testing)

### Don'ts
- Don't use Vite builder in production (unstable)
- Don't skip Controls matchers for colors and dates
- Don't forget to update Storybook when upgrading React
- Don't mix Jest and Vitest in the same config

## Integration with Other Skills

- **react-component-gen**: Use with generated React components
- **mui-theme-helper**: Extracts theme tokens for decorator
- **test-generation**: Auto-generate Jest tests for stories
- **accessibility-audit**: Run axe-core results in CI

